# ============================================================
# CLOUDFLARE PAGES CONFIGURATION
# FILE: _redirects
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS:
#   React Router handles navigation in the browser.
#   But when you visit /men or /product/tee-001 directly
#   (or refresh the page), Cloudflare tries to find an
#   actual file at that path — which doesn't exist.
#
#   This file tells Cloudflare: "For ANY URL that doesn't
#   match a real file, serve index.html instead."
#   Then React Router reads the URL and shows the right page.
#
#   WITHOUT this file: refreshing any page except /
#   would give a 404 error from Cloudflare.
#   WITH this file:    every URL works correctly.
#
# HOW TO USE:
#   Place this file in your project's /public/ folder.
#   Cloudflare Pages automatically reads it after deployment.
# ============================================================

# Redirect all requests to index.html (React handles routing)
/*    /index.html   200
